# The records have left, and three of the four leave the field out. The form that asks the object itself what has become of it is more code than the closed read, so it stands where the text repeats.
# The two functions have one text. A call in a loop enters the first (LinkedFunction::isCalledInLoop): its own body reads by the form. The calls of the second stand outside of loops: its body keeps the closed read.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = GetSlotOrUndefined {{*}}key="aborted"
# RUN(ONCE): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# ONCE-LABEL: code f2:Body
# ONCE: = PropGet {{*}}key="aborted"
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 1 true false
